                <pb facs="0270" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24181: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-05T13:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>278. Department’s 165, June 4, 5 p.m. and Embassy’s 271, June 1, 6 p.m. China is
                    the only Government which has recognized the present administration. Chinese
                    Chargé d’Affaires states that its recognition is <hi rendition="#italic">de
                        facto.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
